(7419528, 1170004, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Decent enough image, good exposure, a little too centred and thus a little too safe for most voters, but still basically a good shot.  Can''t see any screaming flaws.<br/> <br/>I was also wondering why this image is so small, it looks barely even 800p on the long side.  Nice wide angle shot, interesting pov (love that you''re shooting downwards) Could''ve ribboned if, as has already been said, at 1200p on the longest side.  Otherwise so much detail is lost.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful, feel free to pm me<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Decent enough image, good exposure, a little too centred and thus a little too safe for most voters, but still basically a good shot.  Can''t see any screaming flaws. I was also wondering why this image is so small, it looks barely even 800p on the long side.  Nice wide angle shot, interesting pov (love that you''re shooting downwards) Could''ve ribboned if, as has already been said, at 1200p on the longest side.  Otherwise so much detail is lost. Hope this has been helpful, feel free to pm me Susan', '2015-11-30 19:58:40.000000', NULL, 0);
